<title>USA: GTE gets $45.2 mln contract from U.S. Army.</title>
<headline>GTE gets $45.2 mln contract from U.S. Army.</headline>
<dateline>TAUNTON, Mass. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>GTE Corp said Tuesday that it received a $45.2 million contract to integrate technology into the U.S. Army's tactical communications.</p>
<p>GTE said in a release Tuesday that it would apply its asynchronous transfer mode (ATM) technology as a part of the U.S. Army's plans to modernize its communications system.</p>
<p>The ATM upgrade will &quot;permit more efficient use of bandwidth and provide multimedia services of voice, video and data to the battlefield,&quot; GTE said.</p>
</text>
